{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_document", "label": "Scenarios and Data Changes", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each scenario states only the data effect of the proposed design. The exact API is built in the matching roadmap stage."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "label": "Coach Signup", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A normalized phone opens a signup draft and a signup OTP before any user exists. Final signup writes users and only one profile in one transaction, then nulls open_phone. The coach can enter the panel without a paid order. Web login creates a session. Mobile login creates a personal access token. An existing phone or national code fails on the unique constraint so a half-created account does not remain. An athlete panel does not create independent services or a platform payment. A coach's athlete profile is created later, only when they become another coach's athlete."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_plan_purchase", "label": "Plan Purchase and Access Activation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An existing pending order is returned; otherwise the order and feature snapshot are copied from the current plan. Each payment start is a new attempt with a unique idempotency key. The callback locks the attempt. If a payment already exists, nothing new is inserted. The confirmed amount must equal the order price or the attempt fails and no period is created. Success writes one payment, marks the order paid, clears the open-checkout key, and creates one access period. If no other period is active, the new period is active; otherwise it is scheduled to start when the active period ends. Later plan edits do not change snapshotted order rows."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_invite_new_athlete", "label": "Invite Athlete Without an Account", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The coach with an active period records phone, name, and national code. The scenario both says that a missing user causes users, athlete profile, and the relationship to be created in that same transaction with capacity locked there, and later says that OTP acceptance creates the user, profile, active relationship, started event, and accepted invitation. An open invite for the same coach and phone returns the same row via the unique invite key. The period row is lockForUpdate before the relationship insert. Two concurrent creates for a new phone: one creates the user and the other must attach that user to the relationship instead of returning an unfamiliar account error."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_connect_existing_athlete", "label": "Connect Athlete Who Already Has an Account", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The invitation is created for an existing user's phone. Acceptance after OTP finds the user and creates an athlete profile only if missing. If the pair's relationship row exists and is ended, that same row becomes active and a reactivated event is written, subject to capacity. If it is already active, acceptance returns it unchanged. Two coaches inviting the same person create two independent relationships when each has capacity. The existing password is not reset."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_assign_workout", "label": "Create and Assign a Workout Program", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A coach with the workout_programs capability creates a program and a draft version. Publishing freezes those rows. The next edit is a new draft, and current_version_id changes after the new version is published. Assignment points at the published version and the active relationship and creates a program_assigned notification. The old assignment still points at the previous version. Another coach's private exercise cannot be selected."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_log_session", "label": "Log a Session and a Record", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The athlete creates a session with a civil date and, if a relationship is active, that relationship id. Each real attempt is its own set. On set completion the service reads the previous maximum and writes a record event only if the value is greater, linked to that set. estimated_1rm_g is an extra event beside weight and reps. A free session follows the same rule and receives the active relationship id if sent to the coach. Breaking a record notifies the athlete and that relationship's coach. A later program-version change does not rewrite the logged day or sets."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_assign_meal", "label": "Create and Assign a Meal Plan", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A food change gets a new nutrient revision. The previous revision is not updated. Draft items point at the revision current when the item was added. Publishing locks the version. Later food changes attach only future versions to the new revision. Meal assignment points at the relationship and the published version, like workout assignment. Meal calorie totals are not a stored column and are computed on read."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_body_progress", "label": "Body Analysis and Progress Report", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An observation is stored for the measurement time. Only metrics that exist are inserted. If this observation has weight and a height exists here or on the latest earlier observation, a calculated bmi_centi row is added with bmi_v1. Relationship visibility carries the active relationship id and only that coach sees it with the athlete. Progress and Before/After read two times from these rows. No result table is created. A shared observation creates a body_observation_recorded notification."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_ai_publish", "label": "AI Proposal and Publication", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Generative requests are rejected while ai_onboarding_completed_at is empty. Creating a turn locks the active period, increments quota by one, and writes a usage entry. Tools read only that coach_profile_id and the context relationship. Model text is stored on messages. A program output is a draft generation with a proposal and is not assigned. Coach approval builds an ordinary workout or meal version, marks the generation materialized, and stores the version id. Assignment then follows the workout or meal scenario. Rejection marks the generation rejected and builds no version. An athlete can open a conversation only if ai_athlete_access is on the period snapshot, and it spends that coach's quota."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_end_relationship", "label": "End the Coaching Relationship", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The relationship becomes ended, ended_at is filled, and an ended event is inserted. Open invitations and active assignments of that relationship close. Sessions, sets, versions, observations, and messages are not deleted. A new session after this time does not receive this relationship id. The coach may only read messages, progress, and programs of this period. Body photos, including photos from this period, close for the coach and for that coach's AI. Data before started_at and another coach's data stay out of reach. Period capacity frees because only active relationships are counted."}, {"id": "docs_product_04_scenarios_plan_expiry", "label": "Plan Expiry or Plan Change", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A job moves an active period whose ends_at has passed to expired and nulls active_coach_id. A due scheduled period becomes active in the same process if the active key stays unique. After expiry with no replacement, invitations, new assignments, AI generation, and coaching writes are rejected. History remains readable as in the end-relationship scenario. A new plan purchase creates a new order and snapshot. If the proposed policy starts it after the current period, a scheduled period is created. If the new capacity is below the active relationship count, no relationship is automatically ended. A failed payment only marks the attempt failed. The order can accept a new attempt until it expires. A repeated failed callback does not create a payment or a period."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_document", "target": "docs_product_06_roadmap_document", "relation": "cites", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_document", "target": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "target": "docs_product_02_database_signup_drafts", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "target": "docs_product_02_database_otp_challenges", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "target": "docs_product_02_database_users", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "target": "docs_product_02_database_sessions", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_coach_signup", "target": "docs_product_02_database_personal_access_tokens", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/product/04-scenarios.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_product_04_scenarios_document", "target": "docs_product_04_scenarios_plan_purchase", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "